# test/spec/fair/param.cml: the fairness of a parameterized action is
# that of its disjunction, as WF_vars(go) for go == \E i \in 0 .. 1 :
# ...  go(0) flips x for ever, which takes go, so WF on go holds on a
# run that never takes go(1) and never finishes (violated).  Fairness
# per instance would make go(1) fire and the property hold.
module param
var x : 0 .. 1
var done : 0 .. 1
init x == 0 and done == 0
action go(i in 0 .. 1):
  when done == 0
  x' = (1 - x) * (1 - i) + x * i
  done' = i
deadlock = off
fair weak go
property finishes: eventually done == 1
